post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'

SimpleLogin has been installed.

Configuration:
  /etc/simplelogin/simplelogin.env.example

Persistent state:
  /var/lib/simplelogin/pgp
  /var/lib/simplelogin/upload

For a new installation, copy and edit the example configuration before
starting the services.

Migrating an existing Docker installation
-----------------------------------------

Typical Docker paths map as follows:

  SimpleLogin .env
    -> /etc/simplelogin/simplelogin.env

  /sl/pgp
    -> /var/lib/simplelogin/pgp

  /code/static/upload
    -> /var/lib/simplelogin/upload

  DKIM private/public keys
    -> /etc/simplelogin/dkim.key
    -> /etc/simplelogin/dkim.pub.key

Recommended native settings include:

  DB_URI=postgresql://simplelogin@/simplelogin?host=/run/postgresql
  GNUPGHOME=/var/lib/simplelogin/pgp
  DKIM_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=/etc/simplelogin/dkim.key
  DKIM_PUBLIC_KEY_PATH=/etc/simplelogin/dkim.pub.key
  POSTFIX_SERVER=localhost

Optional Valkey over a Unix socket:

  MEM_STORE_URI=redis+unix:///run/valkey/valkey.sock

If using peer PostgreSQL authentication, the Unix service account and
PostgreSQL role should both be named "simplelogin".

When migrating an existing installation, stop the old containers before
the final state copy, then run the database migrations from:

  cd /usr/lib/simplelogin
  sudo -u simplelogin env CONFIG=/etc/simplelogin/simplelogin.env flask db upgrade

Do not run init_app.py against an existing SimpleLogin database.

Services:
  simplelogin.service
  simplelogin-email.service
  simplelogin-job-runner.service

They are not enabled automatically.

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'MSG'

SimpleLogin upgraded.

If this release contains database migrations, run:

  cd /usr/lib/simplelogin
  sudo -u simplelogin env CONFIG=/etc/simplelogin/simplelogin.env flask db upgrade

Review /usr/share/doc/simplelogin-server/example.env for new upstream
configuration options when upgrading between SimpleLogin releases.

MSG
}
